From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carl Su <xuyusu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libdwfl: fix bad fts workaround with external LFS flags

elfutils has a BAD_FTS workaround for older glibc fts.h headers that
cannot be included with large-file support enabled. The workaround
includes fts.h before config.h because config.h may define
_FILE_OFFSET_BITS.

Buildroot passes _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 in CPPFLAGS, so the macro is
already defined before config.h is included. This defeats the BAD_FTS
workaround and fails the build with older glibc soft-float toolchains:

  fts.h:41:3: error: #error "<fts.h> cannot be used with -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS==64"

Temporarily undefine _FILE_OFFSET_BITS around the early fts.h include in
the BAD_FTS path, then restore it for the rest of the translation unit.
This preserves the intent of the existing workaround when large-file
support is injected by the build system instead of config.h.

Upstream: N/A, Buildroot-specific external CPPFLAGS interaction
Signed-off-by: Carl Su <xuyusu@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 libdwfl/linux-kernel-modules.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libdwfl/linux-kernel-modules.c b/libdwfl/linux-kernel-modules.c
index 86c895c..d0601c3 100644
--- a/libdwfl/linux-kernel-modules.c
+++ b/libdwfl/linux-kernel-modules.c
@@ -33,7 +33,15 @@
    contained. */
 #ifdef BAD_FTS
+  #ifdef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+    #define ELFUTILS_RESTORE_FILE_OFFSET_BITS _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+    #undef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+  #endif
   #include <sys/types.h>
   #include <fts.h>
+  #ifdef ELFUTILS_RESTORE_FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+    #define _FILE_OFFSET_BITS ELFUTILS_RESTORE_FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+    #undef ELFUTILS_RESTORE_FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+  #endif
 #endif
 
 #include <config.h>
-- 
2.34.1
